<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pero do Campo Tourinho</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pero do Campo Tourinho was a Portuguese nobleman from Viana do Castelo who received the hereditary Captaincy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> Seguro from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III in 1534. He arrived with settlers in 1535 and founded Porto Seguro and other villages. His settlers denounced him for heresy, and in 1546 he was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> to face the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a>.</p></div>
